{
  "statement": "Ethical and compliance considerations are essential for a bookkeeping system, ensuring it adheres to legal standards and promotes accountability. Requirements RES-01 through RES-07 collectively guarantee compliance with financial regulations, secure access to data, transparent audit trails, fraud detection, and fair reporting practices. These provisions not only protect users but also enhance trust in the system. Without these safeguards, the system risks legal repercussions and reputational damage, undermining its core purpose.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-02", "TRU-06"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "User access controls (TRU-02) might conflict with user access logs (TRU-06), as strict controls could limit necessary oversight for accountability."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["GRN-06"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "The integration of carbon offset options (GRN-06) may create legal complexities regarding user transactions, affecting compliance with financial regulations (RES-01)."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02"],
      "type": "redundant",
      "description": "The requirement for double-entry systems (SAF-02) may overlap with our auditing and accountability goals (RES-03), as both emphasize transaction integrity."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [],
